    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a job data extractor. Your task is to convert the given job posting data into a strict JSON with the following fields (example):\n\n{\n    \"source\": \"linkedin\",\n    \"title\": \"Computer Vision Engineer\",\n    \"company\": \"MedAI Diagnostics\",\n    \"location\": \"Paris, France\",\n    \"salary\": \"45k–60k € / year\",\n    \"job_description_summary\": \"You will develop and optimize image analysis algorithms for detection and segmentation of anomalies in medical imaging modalities (CT/MRI).\",\n    \"profile_skills\": [\n      \"Python\",\n      \"PyTorch\",\n      \"Segmentation\",\n      \"Deep Learning\",\n      \"Computer Vision\"\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://www.welcometothejungle.com/jobs/12345\",\n    \"scraped_at\": \"2025-11-07 07:59:00\"\n}\n\nRules:\n1. Extract information only from the input.\n2. If a field is not present, leave it as an empty string \"\" for strings, or an empty array [] for lists.\n3. Job description summary must be 3 sentences max.\n4. Dates should be in ISO format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS if including time.\n5. Skills should be a concise list of relevant keywords extracted from the job description.\n6. Preserve the field names exactly as shown. Output must be valid JSON ONLY, nothing else: \n   - No explanations  \n   - No markdown  \n   - No leading or trailing quotes  \n   - Output MUST be valid JSON.\n\nCurrent date is: {{ $now }}\n\nHere is the job posting data:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
        4128,
        736
      ],
      "id": "50e22b0c-88ae-4f24-bb31-7c02d17e10c2",
      "name": "LLM Job Data Extractor"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Candidate Profile:\n- Recent graduate (Junior roles or 0-3 years experience roles)\n- Fields: Computer Vision, Image Processing, AI, Machine Learning, Deep Learning, Medical Imaging, Pathology Image, R&D\n- Preferred sectors: Healthcare, Pathology, but open to any sector offering the above fields\n- Also acceptable roles: Data Scientist, Consultant in AI/ML fields\n- Examples of companies: Gleamer, Bioptimus, Sonio, Owkins, Whitelab, Raidium, GE Healthcare, Idemia, HuggingFace, GoPro, Thales, Dassault, SocgenAI, AWS, Datadog, IBM Consulting...\n\nInstructions:\n1. Examine each job in the provided list.\n2. Filter out any jobs that are obviously unrelated to the candidate’s fields or locations.\n3. Keep jobs that match the profile.\n4. Output ONLY a JSON array containing the `id` of each matching job.  \n   - No explanations  \n   - No markdown  \n   - No leading or trailing quotes  \n   - Output MUST be valid JSON.\n\nInput jobs:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json[\"jobs\"]) }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are a job filter assistant. Your role is to read a list of job offers and return only those that match the candidate’s profile.  Always output a JSON format string with array ids of kept jobs.  Do not add explanations or commentary."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
